{#
  EditorialNav. Her name, and the sections. Nothing else.

  No volume number, no issue number, no date line: this is a portfolio under
  her own name, not a journal with back issues.

  DESIGN_SYSTEM.md originally specified a <details>/<summary> disclosure
  below 768px. Dropped, and the spec amended: there are four links, each a
  single short uppercase word. They wrap to two lines at 375px and cost
  nothing. A disclosure would add a control, a state, and a fight with the
  UA stylesheet's closed-state hiding, to save one line of height. The
  native-element rule is about not rebuilding native behaviour with divs —
  it is not a reason to add a widget that is not needed.
#}
<header class="nav">
  <p class="nav__wordmark">
    {% if page.url == "/" %}{{ site.title }}{% else %}<a href="/">{{ site.title }}</a>{% endif %}
  </p>

  <nav class="nav__sections" aria-label="Sections">
    <ul class="nav__list">
      {%- for item in site.nav %}
      <li><a href="{{ item.href }}"{% if item.href.startsWith("/#") == false and page.url.startsWith(item.href) %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ item.label }}</a></li>
      {%- endfor %}
      <li><a href="mailto:{{ site.author.email }}">Contact</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>
</header>
